 "notes": "Set of Black Range lava rocks. It has a ropy pahoehoe slab (about 2.7 x 1.8 x 0.3 m), a 2.7 m boulder, a faceted boulder, a pillar, a spiky scoria rock, a spiky lava bomb and five small rocks (0.7-1 m). Sizes come from the scale bar (1 m is about 181 px). The slab's top-left drawing is a perspective and is left out. The single rock drawings are slightly elevated product shots, treated as front views; their depths are guesses."}
